# Mutual Fund Return Matrix

Google Apps Script bound to one Google Sheet. Local `code.gs` and `index.html` mirror that project. Do not re-ask sheet names, columns, tenures, or entry points.

## Files
- `code.gs` — menu, web app, and calculations.
- `index.html` — UI. Apps Script file name is `Index` (`HtmlService.createTemplateFromFile('Index')`).
- `scheme_codes.csv` / `nav_data.csv` are the sheet sources. Runtime reads the spreadsheet, not the repo files.

## Sheets
- `scheme_codes`: `scheme_code`, `scheme_name`, `amc_name`, `fund_category`, `plan`, `option`, `min_nav_date`
- `nav_data`: `scheme_code`, `scheme_name`, `date`, `nav` (~172k rows). Never load the full CSV into context; sample headers or filter by scheme.

## Two return series
- Tenure columns look back from **Sale Date** on historical NAV. Each tenure has SIP XIRR and trailing CAGR. The toolbar switch chooses which one is shown.
- **Custom Range** uses **From Date** through **To Date** only: Custom Range XIRR, SIP Corpus, Net Profit, Absolute return.

## Defaults
SIP ₹1,000 on the 5th. From Date is today minus 1 year. To Date and Sale Date are today. Top 2 per category by the active 1Y series is on. Category, AMC, and Scheme filters start on Select All.
